TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Reproduced checkpoint cp-proxy's serve failure outside the gate and traced it to a missing ROCm flash-attention implementation inside the flashnext:dev image, not to a defect in the command cp-proxy runs. Evidence, in order:\n- The gate's first half succeeded (make-proxy correctly skipped a rebuild; the checkpoint at /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy was built at 11:13 and matches its signature). The failure is entirely in scripts/run-proxy.sh: the serve container started at 11:25:16 and died 50s later, before answering on :1236.\n- The captured receipt (results/receipts/failed/proxy.json) keeps only the last 20 serve-log lines, which cut off the line the traceback points at ('See root cause above'), so I re-ran the identical podman serve (same image, same env, same argv, port 1237, disposable container, removed afterwards; no repository file touched) and captured the whole log.\n- Root cause, verbatim from that log: '(EngineCore pid=300) NotImplementedError: Qwen4Exp QSA requires FlashAttention', raised at /opt/vllm/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/amd/qsa.py:108 in Qwen4ExpQSAFlashAttentionImpl.__init__, reached through amd/model.py:416 make_layers -> model.py:226 Qwen4ExpDecoderLayer -> qsa.py:279. The engine core dies during load_model, hence the empty 'Failed core proc(s): {}' at the API-server end.\n- The guard is is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available(); on ROCm it returns _ROCM_FLASH_ATTN_AVAILABLE (/opt/vllm/vllm/v1/attention/backends/fa_utils.py:342-372), which needs either aiter.ops.triton.mha or upstream flash_attn. Probed inside the image: 'FA_AVAILABLE: False', 'aiter: No module named aiter', 'flash_attn: No module named flash_attn'; the pinned wheel set carries only torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, triton 3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0, torchvision and conch-triton-kernels. So the capability is simply absent from the image the campaign builds.\n- No knob can route around it: Qwen4ExpQSAAttention.__init__ hardcodes self.impl = Qwen4ExpQSAFlashAttentionImpl (amd/qsa.py:279), with no envs. lookup and no backend selection, so every full_attention (QSA) layer raises at construction regardless of exec mode, VLLM_PLE_MMAP, gpu-memory-utilization or the multimodal limit. The three serve facts run-proxy.sh pins are all correct and irrelevant to this wall.\n- The proxy checkpoint necessarily hits it: scripts/make-proxy.sh:50 picks 4 layers precisely so both attention kinds appear, and the generated config.json carries layer_types ['linear_attention','linear_attention','linear_attention','full_attention'] with full_attention_interval 4, so layer 3 is a QSA layer.\nScope: cp-proxy is a checkpoint whose brief forbids repository changes, and its argv is fixed by the worklist, so there is no fix inside this task; a second attempt would reproduce this byte for byte. The machinery is healthy (image built at 11:24:29 before the run, receipt quarantined under results/receipts/failed/ per doctrine, container reaped cleanly), so this is not a transient fault either. The fix belongs to the container lane (container-recipe): flashnext:dev must ship a working ROCm flash_attn_varlen_func. Shrinking the proxy to 3 layers would make cp-proxy green while hiding the same wall from cp-tp2, whose real workload config is 48 layers at full_attention_interval 4 and would die identically; that trade should not be taken silently. Separately worth fixing in the proxy-tooling lane when it next opens: run-proxy.sh's 20-line serve_log_tail discards the one line that names the cause, which is why this diagnosis needed a re-run to recover it.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["container/Containerfile","container/build.sh","scripts/build-engine.sh","results/receipts/build.json"],"goal":"Give flashnext:dev a working ROCm flash_attn_varlen_func so the fork's Qwen4Exp QSA attention can construct on gfx1151. Add to the pinned wheel set (container/Containerfile, container/build.sh) either aiter with aiter.ops.triton.mha or an upstream flash-attn build for ROCm 7.14 / torch 2.13, so that vllm.v1.attention.backends.fa_utils.is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available() returns True inside the image, then rebuild through scripts/build-engine.sh and refresh results/receipts/build.json with the new image digest. Do not change the proxy shape to dodge this: dropping the full_attention layer from the proxy would only defer the identical NotImplementedError to cp-tp2 on the real workload. If no ROCm flash-attention wheel can be pinned for this substrate, stop and report that, because it is a campaign-level blocker for every serve of a checkpoint with full_attention layers, not just for the proxy.","acceptance":[{"id":"fa-varlen-available","description":"The image reports a working ROCm flash_attn_varlen_func, which is the exact predicate the fork's QSA impl checks.","argv":["bash","-euc","podman run --rm flashnext:dev python3 -c \"from vllm.v1.attention.backends.fa_utils import is_flash_attn_varlen_func_available as f; assert f(), 'ROCm flash_attn_varlen_func still unavailable'; print('FA varlen available')\""]},{"id":"proxy-first-light","description":"The cp-proxy command itself passes end to end: the proxy checkpoint builds or is reused, the serve answers on :1236, and the receipt lands as status=pass rather than under results/receipts/failed/.","argv":["bash","-euc","bash scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/run-proxy.sh && test -f results/receipts/proxy.json && ! test -f results/receipts/failed/proxy.json"]},{"id":"receipts-and-build-digest","description":"The graded receipt ladder still validates and the build receipt names the image that was actually tested.","argv":["bash","-euc","python3 scripts/receipts-verify.py && python3 -c \"import json,subprocess; d=json.load(open('results/receipts/build.json'))['data']['image_digest'].split(':')[-1]; got=subprocess.run(['podman','inspect','--format','{{.Id}}','flashnext:dev'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip(); assert got==d, (got,d); print('build receipt matches the tagged image')\""]}],"dependencies":["container-recipe"]}}
